From b799ac6509a9dcc16f9671ddf2d65e7c3a23ab09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bobsixsixsix-boop <304558835+bobsixsixsix-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:33:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: baldur-audio: enable the aw882xx volume
 fade

The out-of-tree aw882xx driver (v1.15.0) only ramps the amplifier's
digital volume on start/stop when the DT says fade-flag = <1>
(aw882xx_device.c aw_device_parse_fade_flag_dt; default 0, the boot log
says 'fade-flag: 0'). Without it aw882xx_dev_mute() releases and sets
HMUTE at the full aw_dev_N_volume gain, so any non-zero sample at that
instant becomes a step.

With the flag, aw_dev_reg_fw_update() parks the volume at the mute
value, device_start() ramps it up after HMUTE is released (16 steps of
64 x 0.094 dB, 100 us apart by default, about 5 ms with the I2C
writes) and device_stop() ramps it down before HMUTE (500 us apart,
about 10-13 ms per amplifier, run in hw_free). aw_dev_N_volume keeps
working as before; aw882xx_fadein_us / aw882xx_fadeout_us and the
fade_step sysfs file tune the ramp at run time.

Not verified on hardware: whether the analog power-stage transitions
(AMPPD/PWDN) themselves click is not affected by this change.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-audio.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-audio.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-audio.dtsi
index f9ab99f..63a0332 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-audio.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-audio.dtsi
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@
 		aw-re-max = <30000>;
 		rename-flag = <1>;
 		sync-load = <1>;
+		/*
+		 * Ramp the amplifier's digital volume on every start/stop
+		 * (aw_dev_fade_in/out: mute volume <-> aw_dev_N_volume in
+		 * 64-step increments). Without it the driver flips HMUTE
+		 * at full gain; the vendor default is off.
+		 */
+		fade-flag = <1>;
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 	};
 
@@ -43,6 +50,7 @@
 		aw-re-max = <30000>;
 		rename-flag = <1>;
 		sync-load = <1>;
+		fade-flag = <1>;
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 	};
 };
